::SPEECH_U05_L08_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L08_GuidedPractice_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.03
Question:
Unit 5 synthesis: Which choice best improves a publication-ready speech product?
{
~A. Publish the first draft without reviewing it#This choice is incomplete because it does not support clear publication, revision, audience awareness, or digital presentation quality.
~B. Add more decoration instead of improving meaning#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully meet the communication purpose or collaboration standard.
=C. Revise wording, organize slides, and check final publication quality#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L08_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L08_GuidedPractice_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.04
Question:
Which choice best combines revision and slide design?
{
=A. Use feedback to clarify speaker notes and reduce crowded slide text#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~B. Add more decoration instead of improving meaning#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully meet the communication purpose or collaboration standard.
~C. Ignore audience needs during final review#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck revision, publication readiness, audience impact, or slide coherence.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
